# A film folder commits its sources, its lock files AND its final audio:
# narration/*.mp3 with each take's .verify.json and .alignment.json, and
# music/*.mp3. ElevenLabs v3/v4 take no seed, so a re-voiced take is a
# different read and a recomposed score a different piece: the lock files
# record how the audio was made but cannot bring it back, and re-making it
# costs credits. With the audio committed, any clone re-renders or edits a
# scene for free (npm run narrate voices nothing).
#
# Keeping audio out of a public repository? Add narration/*.mp3,
# narration/*.verify.json and music/*.mp3 here; renders then come out silent
# (captions kept) until npm run narrate and npm run music are re-run.
node_modules/
out/
preview/
auditions/
brand-tokens.resolved.json
.env
sfx/*.wav
# Footage frames, rebuilt by npm run clips from clips.json and media.lock.json.
# media/ (the footage itself) is yours to decide: commit what you own and is
# small; keep large or third-party files out and note where they live.
clips/
study/
# Many projects ignore lib/ as build output; these are the film's sources.
!lib/
